al products. Recruits IRAK1 to the IL-1 receptor complex (PubMed:10854325). Inhibits IRAK1 phosphorylation and kinase activity (PubMed:11751856). Connects the ubiquitin pathway to autophagy by functioning as a ubiquitin-ATG8 family adapter and thus mediating autophagic clearance of ubiquitin conjugates (PubMed:25042851). The TOLLIP-dependent selective autophagy pathway plays an important role in clearance of cytotoxic polyQ proteins aggregates (PubMed:25042851). In a complex with TOM1, recruits ubiquitin-conjugated proteins onto early endosomes (PubMed:15047686). Binds to phosphatidylinositol 3-phosphate (PtdIns(3)P) (PubMed:26320582)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}